# Keep the Docker build context small — every file listed below is either
# regenerated inside the image OR a secret that must not leak in.

# Dependencies — installed fresh inside the image
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Local + CI ephemera
.git
.github
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS junk
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test + dev-only
coverage
.nyc_output
*.log

# Build / runtime artefacts
logs
uploads
tmp

# Repo-only docs, scripts, migrations (the ones that need to be available
# IN the image are explicitly named — keeping the rest out reduces context
# size and image rebuild churn).
#
# Caveat on `docs/`: the directory now holds BOTH operational markdown
# guides (AWS_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md, ENV_VARS.md, GITHUB_SECRETS.md — all
# image-irrelevant) AND **runtime code** added 2026-05-25 for the
# Swagger autogen (`docs/swagger.js`, `docs/openapi-autogen.js`,
# `docs/openapi.yaml`). Excluding the directory wholesale used to be
# safe; now it'd ship a broken image because `server.js` requires
# `./docs/swagger` at boot. Narrow the exclusion to .md files inside
# docs/ so the JS + YAML files get included.
docs/**/*.md
*.md
nodemon.json
ecosystem.config.js
deploy
